  "markdown_content": "## Deal overview\\n\\nITC has agreed to acquire 24 Mantra Organic, an organic FMCG staples brand, for a consideration of \u20b9472.5 crore, according to a report by CNBC TV18 dated April 17, 2025.\\n\\n## Strategic rationale\\n\\nThe announcement marks a strategic move by ITC to broaden its footprint in the organic and health-focused foods category. ITC has been steadily expanding its consumer foods portfolio in recent years as it looks to strengthen offerings to health-conscious shoppers.\\n\\n## About ITC\\n\\nITC is a diversified Indian conglomerate with an established presence in:\\n- cigarettes\\n- hotels\\n- paperboards and packaging\\n- agribusiness\\n- fast-moving consumer goods\\n\\n## About 24 Mantra Organic\\n\\n24 Mantra Organic is positioned in the organic staples and packaged foods market, catering to consumers seeking organic and natural food options. The brand\u2019s product range and distribution network in the organic segment are likely to be key assets for ITC.\\n\\n## Industry impact and analyst view\\n\\nIndustry analysts expect the acquisition to provide ITC with greater access to the fast-growing organic foods market in India, where demand has been rising alongside increased awareness of health and sustainability. The deal may also offer:\\n- supply-chain synergies\\n- opportunities to scale the brand using ITC\u2019s distribution and marketing capabilities\\n\\n## Financial and regulatory details\\n\\nFinancial and operational details beyond the headline consideration were limited in the initial report. The companies will likely complete customary regulatory and closing formalities before integrating the business into ITC\u2019s consumer products operations.\\n\\n## Sector context\\n\\nThe transaction underscores continuing consolidation in the Indian FMCG sector as larger players acquire niche and premium brands to diversify portfolios and capture changing consumer preferences.\\n\\n> CNBC TV18 reported the development on April 17, 2025.",
